# Project layout lessons

<!-- PROJECT-LAYOUT-LESSONS -->
### midi-dense-routing-and-labels
- **Trigger:** Rotating MIDI protection parts and replacing axial ferrites in a smaller layout
- **Rule:** Recompute fixed cathode routes from actual pad positions; do not cross the other diode terminal. Inset the router work area to preserve native edge clearance. Reserve the full DIP body envelope when placing neighboring value labels.
- **Evidence:** review/layout-notes.md
- **Check:** Native DRC/parity zero including 3mm rule; separate 100n labels beside their rows; no labels inside another body.

